## Outcome

A fresh generated Waaseyaa application must prove the developer journey and security ownership model end to end, not merely boot.

## Required acceptance journey

From a clean packaged `composer create-project` consumer:

1. initialize the selected site profile;
2. install/migrate through the governed lifecycle;
3. register or create an account according to policy;
4. verify email where configured;
5. log in and log out with session rotation and CSRF protection intact;
6. request and complete a password reset;
7. configure and verify 2FA, including the pending-login path and recovery behavior;
8. update application-owned profile data;
9. exercise one consumer extension recipe;
10. publish/customize account UI and detect a simulated upstream change;
11. update the Framework dependency and prove package-owned security behavior changes without re-copying consumer backend code.

